<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: HORSE RACING-RESULTS OF FEATURE RACES AT LEOPARDSTOWN.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-RESULTS OF FEATURE RACES AT LEOPARDSTOWN.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of feature races at</p>
<p>Leopardstown on Friday.</p>
<p>McCain Handicap steeplechase run over two miles and two</p>
<p>furlongs (3.4-km).</p>
<p>1. Merry Gale (5-4) ridden by Richard Dunwoody.</p>
<p>2. Klairon Davis (5-4 ON favourite) Francis Woods.</p>
<p>3. Fiftysevenchannels (8-1) Charlie Swan.</p>
<p>Five ran.</p>
<p>Distances: Eight lengths, 13 lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Herb Stanley and trained by Jim Dreaper in</p>
<p>County Dublin.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 6,850 Irish punts ($11,350)</p>
<p>First Choice Novice hurdle run over two miles and</p>
<p>two furlongs (3.4-km).</p>
<p>1. Istabraq (10-3 ON favourite) Charlie Swan.</p>
<p>2. Palette (100-30) David Casey.</p>
<p>3. Delphi Lodge (10-1) Tony Martin.</p>
<p>Five ran.</p>
<p>Distances: Five and a half lengths, one length.</p>
<p>Winner owned by John McManus and trained by Aidan O'Brien in</p>
<p>County Kilkenny.</p>
<p>Value to winner 9,675 Irish punts ($16,000)</p>
<p>Paddy Power Handicap steeplechase run over three miles</p>
<p>(4.8-km).</p>
<p>1. New Co (11-4 favourite) Conor O'Dwyer.</p>
<p>2. Wylde Hide (8-1) Francis Woods.</p>
<p>3. Time For A Run (6-1) Richard Dunwoody.</p>
<p>17 ran.</p>
<p>Distances: One length, seven lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by the Ronan family and trained by Mouse Morris</p>
<p>in County Tipperary.</p>
<p>Value to winner 44,050 Irish punts ($73,000).</p>
</text>
